  "limits": [
    "Original application coverage on the private cross-host path is the signed-out ChatGPT Linux client, including a native form. Account sign-in, conversations and Claude Artifacts remain unverified.",
    "Typing and IME commits stay bound to the original focus, editor contents and selection. The cloud adapter dispatches a cancellable beforeinput event synchronously (isTrusted is false), then invokes Chromium’s native editing command. Chromium’s resulting input event is trusted and can be undone. A web editor requiring a trusted beforeinput event needs separate validation.",
    "Control sampling on animated surfaces is bounded. When the original and current hit cannot be certified and the scene has changed, the client rejects the click and the user can inspect the updated surface.",
    "The supported desktop app captures use SkPicture v110, supported Viz passes and verified fonts. Windows 11 display, focus and Microsoft IME remain unverified."
  ],
